From: SenkOS
Subject: [PATCH] h265decoder: start a new bitstream on flush

After a flushing seek the stream resumes at a key unit, which can be a CRA.
new_bitstream stayed FALSE, so the CRA got NoRaslOutputFlag = 0 and its RASL
pictures were decoded against references that are not in the DPB. On Cedrus
(v4l2slh265dec) the engine then reads stale reference addresses: an IOMMU
fault, a request that never completes, and "Not enough memory to decode H265
stream".

Upstream-Status: Pending

---
--- a/gst-libs/gst/codecs/gsth265decoder.c
+++ b/gst-libs/gst/codecs/gsth265decoder.c
@@ -1340,6 +1340,10 @@
   GstH265Decoder *self = GST_H265_DECODER (decoder);
 
   gst_h265_decoder_clear_dpb (self, TRUE);
+  /* After a seek a CRA starts a new bitstream: its RASL pictures reference
+   * pictures that were never decoded and must be dropped (8.1.3) */
+  self->priv->new_bitstream = TRUE;
+  self->priv->prev_nal_is_eos = FALSE;
 
   return TRUE;
 }
